    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n103434" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τετρα-λογία</span></b> , ἡ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a group of four</i> Platonic <i>dialogues</i>, Thrasyll.
			ap. <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				3.57
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				9.45
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a group</i> or <i>series of four dramas</i>, three Tragedies
			and one Satyric play (or sts. four Tragedies), <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				619
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.L.
				3.56
			</span></i>.</div>
